     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia sets aside ten percent of its $242 million pledge to the Global Fund&apos;s sixth replenishment to provide targeted support for Indo-Pacific countries. This includes funding to strengthen laboratory and diagnostic capacity in Cambodia, Laos and PNG through the &apos;IndoPacLab&apos; project. In Laos, IndoPacLab worked closely with the National Centre for Laboratory and Epidemiology and Ministry of Health on implementing a national system to standardize and streamline lab processes and data management. In 2023, this resulted in IndoPac Lab supporting a Laboratory Information Management System (LIMS) pilot in 3 laboratories across Laos that strengthened laboratory data and supply chain management. The support of the IndoPac Lab project consequently catalysed a further $2 million investment from the Global Fund to scale-up the LIMS to all provinces (2024-2026) to enhance the quality and timeliness of data to inform public health decisions and improve patient care across Laos.</narrative>
